Description: Selection of survey samples by Chromy's method of sequential
    random sampling with probability minimum replacement, the procedure
    behind 'PROC SURVEYSELECT' 'METHOD=PPS_SEQ': each unit's realised
    number of selections differs from its expected number by less than
    one, and the sample size is always exact. With it, the apparatus the
    method is used with in practice: hierarchical serpentine sorting of
    the frame for implicit stratification; a maximal size measure over
    several auxiliary variables; the allocation that equalises
    anticipated coefficients of variation across variables; expected
    hits with certainty units resolved by iteration or, under minimum
    replacement, units selected more than once; and the multiplicity
    estimator with the successive-difference variance. The computational
    engine is the Rust crate 'chromy-core'. The methods follow Chromy
    (1979) and Chauvet and Le Gleut (2021) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1912.10896>
    for the selection, and Folsom, Potter and Williams (1987) for the
    composite size measure.
